      "statement": "The anything-play enhancement is unified under the single RandomEnhanceMode enum (OFF / TIME_SLOT / EXPLORE, three mutually-exclusive states): PlayerSettingsRepository.randomEnhanceMode prefers the random_enhance_mode DataStore string key and falls back (legacy users) to the mood_time_slot_enabled boolean (true → TIME_SLOT, else OFF); moodTimeSlotEnabled is derived as randomEnhanceMode.map { it == TIME_SLOT }, setRandomEnhanceMode writes both keys in one edit, and PlayerRuntime wires the facade's moodSlotEnabled/exploreModeEnabled lambdas not to per-draw DataStore reads but to the @Volatile randomEnhanceModeCache (seeded once at startup in start() then kept fresh by observeMoodSlotCaches), giving zero-IO per-draw mode evaluation consistent with the UI's isExploreModeActive.",
